{"diagnosis": "Loopback UART RX got 0xff instead of expected 0xa5, i.e. receiver sampled only idle-high bits and missed the start/data frame. Trace shows FAIL 0xdead with TRAP uart data mismatch. Root cause in excerpt is line 114 `send_pattern <= ~1` which drives `ser_tx = send_pattern[0]` low during reset instead of idle-high, corrupting framing for the following dummy and data transmission.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -113,5 +113,5 @@
 		if (!resetn) begin
-			send_pattern <= ~1;
+			send_pattern <= ~0;
 			send_bitcnt <= 0;
 			send_divcnt <= 0;
 			send_dummy <= 1;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (vs FAIL 0xdead), TRAP uart data mismatch gone, loopback recv 0xa5 matches send 0xa5"}

